p
-value. VIP refers to the PLS-DA model Variable Importance in the Project [
123
]. VIP value indicates the contribution of metabolites to the grouping group; The FC (Fold Change) refers to the difference between the difference, which is the ratio of the average value of all biological quantities in each metabolites in the comparison group;
p
-Value obtained [
124
] through T-test calculation, indicating a significant difference in differences. DEMs were screened according to the criteria of VIP > 1.0, FC > 1.5 or FC < 0.667 with
p
-value < 0.05 [
